{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>הנה נא ידעתי.</b> Its midrash: until now he did not recognize her beauty, because of the modesty maintained by both of them; but now he recognized it through an incident. Another interpretation: it is the way of the world that through the hardship of travel a person becomes unkempt, yet she remained in her beauty. And the plain sense of the verse: הנה נא — the time has arrived to fear for your beauty. 'I have known' — I have known this for many days, that you are beautiful of appearance, and now we are coming among people who are dark and ugly, kinsmen of the Cushites, who are not accustomed to a beautiful woman. It is like ״הנה נא אדני סורו נא״ (Genesis 19)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:26.389693892Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}